 # MLPRender_Fea
 
-Also called: Color MLP pipeline, Color Prediction Pipeline, MLP Render, MLP Render with Feature Encoding, MLP Render with Feature and View Positional Encoding, MLP Render with Features, MLP for volume rendering, Neural Radiance Fields network
+Also called: MLP Render with Features, MLP Render with Feature Encoding
 
 ## Overview
-MLPRender_Fea is a neural rendering module that predicts RGB color from input features, view directions, and optional positional encodings using a Multi-Layer Perceptron (MLP) [S3, S7, unofficial]. It solves the problem of mapping continuous spatial features to view-dependent radiance values in neural implicit representations [S7, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from its parent [NeRF MLP Architecture](910-nerf-mlp-architecture.md) by explicitly decoupling the input representation: it accepts pre-computed features (rather than raw 3D coordinates) as primary input, while still processing view directions to model appearance variations [S7, unofficial]. Unlike [NeRF with Per-Image Embeddings](2484-nerf-with-per-image-embeddings.md) which injects global scene context, MLPRender_Fea focuses on local feature-to-color mapping [S7, unofficial].
+MLPRender_Fea is a neural rendering module that predicts RGB color from input features and view directions using a Multi-Layer Perceptron (MLP) [S3, S8, unofficial]. It solves the problem of mapping continuous spatial features to view-dependent radiance values in neural implicit representations [S3, S8, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from its parent [NeRF MLP Architecture](910-nerf-mlp-architecture.md) by accepting pre-computed features as primary input instead of raw 3D coordinates, while still processing view directions to model appearance variations [S3, S8, unofficial]. Unlike [NeRF with Per-Image Embeddings](2484-nerf-with-per-image-embeddings.md) which injects global scene context, MLPRender_Fea focuses on local feature-to-color mapping [S1].
 
